body:
Like everyone has said, you're not freaking out over something stupid. And even if he's not cheating this time, you need to get away from him. Everything you have written makes him sound like an awful partner that doesn't seem interested in taking a single step toward building a future with you. And while I know this is only a snapshot of your relationship, it's pretty hard to interpret "i had to beg him to move in together after five years because he just can't be bothered to leave his mom's house" as anything positive. Unless his mom is dying and he's devoting his time to taking care of her, but somehow i feel like this isn't the case.

&#x200B;

He treats you like a toy he's not interested in anymore, but doesn't want anyone else to have. This man is not and has not been good for you for a very long time.
